From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a service's later threads start on its own desktop, not on the user's

A process started on a station that services.exe names in lpDesktop
(__wineservice_winstation\Default) got its default desktop at creation from
the parent when that station handle was inherited or not yet made:
WinSta0\Default. winstation_init then moved the first thread to its own
desktop, but set_thread_desktop only fills a missing process default, so every
later thread (a service's ServiceMain) started on the user's desktop. A
ServiceMain that made any window forced a desktop window with no display there
(the process station says "service"), WinSta0 never got an explorer, and every
program after it failed with "The explorer process failed to start".
set_thread_desktop now also replaces a default desktop that lies outside the
process station. Seen with Glary Utilities (GUBootService, GUMemfilesService).
---
diff --git a/server/winstation.c b/server/winstation.c
index 7d7a945..38b84b6 100644
--- a/server/winstation.c
+++ b/server/winstation.c
@@ -892,8 +892,32 @@ DECL_HANDLER(set_thread_desktop)
         reply->locator = get_shared_object_locator( new_desktop->shared );
     }
 
-    if (!current->process->desktop)
-        set_process_default_desktop( current->process, new_desktop, req->handle );
+    /* The process default desktop is what every later thread starts on. It is
+     * picked at process creation, and when the station named in lpDesktop does
+     * not exist yet (or a station handle was inherited), it is the parent's:
+     * services.exe's WinSta0\Default. The process then creates its own station
+     * and desktop here, and only the calling thread moved. A service's
+     * ServiceMain thread came up on WinSta0\Default, believed itself a service
+     * (the process station says so) and forced a display-less desktop window
+     * into the user's desktop, which then never got an explorer: every program
+     * after it failed with "The explorer process failed to start". A default
+     * desktop outside the process station is never right; follow the thread. */
+    {
+        unsigned int err = get_error();
+        struct desktop *def = NULL;
+
+        if (current->process->desktop &&
+            !(def = get_desktop_obj( current->process, current->process->desktop, 0 )))
+            clear_error();
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_SVC_DESKTOP_STALE
+        if (!current->process->desktop)
+#else
+        if (!def || def->winstation != winstation)
+#endif
+            set_process_default_desktop( current->process, new_desktop, req->handle );
+        if (def) release_object( def );
+        set_error( err );
+    }
 
     if (old_desktop != new_desktop && current->queue) detach_thread_input( current );
 
